AI ASSISTANCE — PLEASE READ
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Substantial parts of this project were written with the help of a large
language model used as a coding agent (OpenCode with a chat model, plus an
image model for a failed logo attempt that was then replaced by hand-drawn
SVG).  That covers, approximately:

  * most of the Python code in lib/ and lib/chat/,
  * the web window (lib/chat/webui/: HTML, CSS, vanilla JS, service worker),
  * the test suites in tests/,
  * the documentation in README.md, docs/ and this NOTICE,
  * the mascot and launcher icon (docs/logo-jmp.svg, docs/logo-jmp.png,
    julians-music-app.svg), drawn as hand-written SVG by the agent.

The human author directed the work, chose the behaviour, ran and read the
tests, reviewed the diffs and is the person answerable for what ships.  The
AI was a tool, not an author.

What this means for the licence and for you:

